{"type":"text","timestamp":1794567515881,"sessionID":"ses_e2b7162e1ffepACOlFctQOU9iv","part":{"id":"prt_1d48ef22100115CBocQe5Ed1S1","messageID":"msg_1d48eb002001sxg74ql8Tk2uuj","sessionID":"ses_e2b7162e1ffepACOlFctQOU9iv","type":"text","text":"Let me understand the bug better. The `cmd_check_anchors` function processes anchor files that exist, but doesn't verify that every range head (from sigstore attestations) has a corresponding `.ots` file.\n","time":{"start":1794567500321,"end":1794567515879}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794567515902,"sessionID":"ses_e2b7162e1ffepACOlFctQOU9iv","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call-e91f4002-a301-4282-a97a-c6088524d686","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/record/record.py","newString":"covered, changes, prev_commit = 0, [], None\n    for lo, hi, commit in sorted(ranges):\n        if lo != covered + 1:\n            bad.append(f\"the writer's ranges {'overlap' if lo <= covered else 'leave a gap'} at entry {min(lo, covered + 1)}\")\n        covered = max(covered, hi)\n        ots_path = os.path.join(a.ledger, \"anchors\", f\"{hi:06d}.ots\")\n        if not os.path.exists(ots_path):\n            bad.append(f\"{hi:06d}.ots is missing\")\n        if prev_commit:  # did the writer's code change between these two runs? (information: a stranger reads the diff)\n            changes.append({\"entries\": f\"{lo}-{hi}\", \"from_commit\": prev_commit, \"to_commit\": commit,\n                            \"writer_code_changed\": _code_changed(a, prev_commit, commit)})\n        prev_commit = commit\n    if covered < len(chain):\n        bad.append(f\"entries {covered + 1}-{len(chain)} were never attested by the writer\")","oldString":"covered, changes, prev_commit = 0, [], None\n    for lo, hi, commit in sorted(ranges):\n        if lo != covered + 1:\n            bad.append(f\"the writer's ranges {'overlap' if lo <= covered else 'leave a gap'} at entry {min(lo, covered + 1)}\")\n        covered = max(covered, hi)\n        if prev_commit:  # did the writer's code change between these two runs? (information: a stranger reads the diff)\n            changes.append({\"entries\": f\"{lo}-{hi}\", \"from_commit\": prev_commit, \"to_commit\": commit,\n                            \"writer_code_changed\": _code_changed(a, prev_commit, commit)})\n        prev_commit = commit\n    if covered < len(chain):\n        bad.append(f\"entries {covered + 1}-{len(chain)} were never attested by the writer\")"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /workspace/record/record.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/record/record.py\n+++ /workspace/record/record.py\n@@ -412,8 +412,11 @@\n for lo, hi, commit in sorted(ranges):\n     if lo != covered + 1:\n         bad.append(f\"the writer's ranges {'overlap' if lo <= covered else 'leave a gap'} at entry {min(lo, covered + 1)}\")\n     covered = max(covered, hi)\n+    ots_path = os.path.join(a.ledger, \"anchors\", f\"{hi:06d}.ots\")\n+    if not os.path.exists(ots_path):\n+        bad.append(f\"{hi:06d}.ots is missing\")\n     if prev_commit:  # did the writer's code change between these two runs? (information: a stranger reads the diff)\n         changes.append({\"entries\": f\"{lo}-{hi}\", \"from_commit\": prev_commit, \"to_commit\": commit,\n                         \"writer_code_changed\": _code_changed(a, prev_commit, commit)})\n     prev_commit = commit\n","filediff":{"file":"/workspace/record/record.py","patch":"Index: /workspace/record/record.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/record/record.py\n+++ /workspace/record/record.py\n@@ -412,8 +412,11 @@\n for lo, hi, commit in sorted(ranges):\n     if lo != covered + 1:\n         bad.append(f\"the writer's ranges {'overlap' if lo <= covered else 'leave a gap'} at entry {min(lo, covered + 1)}\")\n     covered = max(covered, hi)\n+    ots_path = os.path.join(a.ledger, \"anchors\", f\"{hi:06d}.ots\")\n+    if not os.path.exists(ots_path):\n+        bad.append(f\"{hi:06d}.ots is missing\")\n     if prev_commit:  # did the writer's code change between these two runs? (information: a stranger reads the diff)\n         changes.append({\"entries\": f\"{lo}-{hi}\", \"from_commit\": prev_commit, \"to_commit\": commit,\n                         \"writer_code_changed\": _code_changed(a, prev_commit, commit)})\n     prev_commit = commit\n","additions":3,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"workspace/record/record.py","time":{"start":1794567515877,"end":1794567515889}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now I understand the codebase. Let me analyze the bug:\n\nThe bug is in `cmd_check_anchors` function. It iterates through files in the `anchors` directory that match the pattern `ANCHOR_NAME` (which is `([0-9]{6})\\.(sigstore\\.json|ots)`). For each file, it processes either `.ots` or `.sigstore.json` files.\n\nThe issue is: when there's a `.sigstore.json` file that attests a range ending at entry N (e.g., `anchors/000002.sigstore.json`), the code expects there to be a corresponding `.ots` file (e.g., `anchors/000002.ots`) for the range head. But the current code only checks files that actually exist in the anchors directory. If the `.ots` file is missing, it's simply not processed, and no error is reported.\n\nThe fix should be: after processing all the sigstore anchors and collecting the ranges, we should check that for each range head (the `to_seq` of each range), there's a corresponding `.ots` file present.\n\nLet me look at the code more carefully:\n\nIn `cmd_check_anchors`:\n1. It lists all anchor files matching the pattern\n2. For each file, if it's `.ots`, it checks the proof; if it's `.sigstore.json`, it verifies the sigstore bundle and extracts the range\n3. It collects ranges from sigstore anchors\n4. It checks that ranges cover 1..head with no gaps or overlaps\n\nThe bug: It doesn't verify that for each range head (each `hi` in the ranges), there's a corresponding `.ots` file.\n\nThe fix: After collecting the ranges, check that for each range head `hi`, the file `anchors/{hi:06d}.ots` exists. If not, add to `bad` list with message like `000002.ots is missing`.\n\nLet me implement this fix.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1d48f2edf001shPHU1K267Aa1n","sessionID":"ses_e2b7162e1ffepACOlFctQOU9iv","messageID":"msg_1d48eb002001sxg74ql8Tk2uuj"}}
